# ~/.hermes/.env  —  copy this, fill it in, then: chmod 600 ~/.hermes/.env
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy of this file anywhere. This template contains
# variable NAMES only and that is the only version that belongs in git.
#
# Hermes can read this file. Only put things in it that the agent needs.
# The Pinecone key deliberately does NOT live here — see the note at the bottom.

# ── Telegram ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From @BotFather on Telegram: /newbot, then copy the token it gives you.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Comma-separated numeric Telegram user IDs allowed to talk to this bot.
# Get yours by messaging @userinfobot. Leave nobody else in here.
# This is the ONLY thing standing between a stranger and the person's memory.
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=

# ── Vault ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The path INSIDE the container. Don't change it — the mount handles the rest.
OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=/vault

# Where the agent stages notes it wants remembered. Inside the container.
HERMES_INBOX=/opt/data/inbox

# ── Optional integrations ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only add what this specific person actually uses. Every key here is a key the
# agent can read, so an empty file is a safer file.

# AIRTABLE_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_TOKEN=


# ── Deliberately NOT here ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# PINECONE_API_KEY lives at  ~/.hermes/secrets/pinecone.key  (mode 600) instead.
#
# Why: the promoter needs write access to the index, but the agent only ever
# needs to search it. Keeping the key in a file the promoter reads — rather than
# in the environment the agent inherits — means a prompt injection can't exfiltrate
# a credential that could wipe the index.
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.hermes/secrets
#   printf '%s' 'pcsk_your_key_here' > ~/.hermes/secrets/pinecone.key
#   chmod 600 ~/.hermes/secrets/pinecone.key
#
# Model credentials are NOT here either — `hermes model` writes them to
# ~/.hermes/auth.json via an OAuth device flow. Never paste a model key into this file.
